// PIN (GREEN — behavior): fmt:ln over the 4096 scratch buffer must fail
// LOUDLY, not silently empty. The old `catch ""` made a 5K line format to
// empty — the blank-pane class of silent wrong answer (found 2026-09-06 in
// the d_turns dump test, which routed around it via fmt.blk). Now the panic
// names the remedy: use fmt.blk (allocates, no cap).
import std/io
import std/fmt
import std/string
std/string:from-page(text: "")
| ok s |> std/fmt:ln("{{ s:S }}"): l |> std/io:print.ln("UNREACHABLE:{{ l.text:s }}") |> std/string:free(s)
| err _ |> _
